# GnuChanTerm's own terminfo entry.
#
# A terminal's name is a promise and this file is the promise written down.
# Programs do not read the escape sequences out of a manual; they look the name
# up in this database and use what it says. A name with no entry resolves to
# `dumb` — no colour, no cursor addressing, no screen handling — and a program
# that gets `dumb` behaves as if the terminal were a printer.
#
# WHAT IS CLAIMED HERE, AND WHAT IS NOT
#
# Everything below is implemented by term_vt.c and nothing else is listed. That
# is the whole discipline of this file: a capability claimed here and not
# implemented is a program sending a sequence into a terminal that ignores it,
# which shows up as a wrong screen rather than as an error. The safe direction
# is to claim less.
#
# NOT claimed, and why:
#
#   memory_lock / meml    no hardware status line
#   xterm's mouse caps    the SGR mouse protocol is implemented but ncurses
#                         reads it through kmous, which is listed; the rest of
#                         xterm's private extensions are not
#   OSC 52 clipboard      not implemented
#   SIXEL / ReGIS         not implemented
#
# The compiler is `tic -x`, which is what the makefile runs.

gcl-256color|GnuChanTerm|GnuchanOS terminal,
	am,			# automatic margins: writing past the last column wraps
	bce,			# a blank paints the current background
	ccc,			# colours can be changed with initc, which OSC 4 does
	mir,			# safe to move in insert mode
	msgr,			# safe to move while in standout mode
	xenl,			# newline clears to end of line (this terminal does)
	colors#256,
	pairs#32767,
	cols#80,
	it#8,			# tab stops every eight columns
